# Commit Often

## Rule

After completing any meaningful unit of work, **commit and push to `main`** so Vercel auto-deploys.

A "meaningful unit" includes:
- A new or updated component, page, or layout
- A bug fix or style change
- New or updated content (blog posts, case studies, copy changes)
- Config or dependency changes
- Any change the user asks to see live

## How

1. Stage only the relevant files (`git add <files>`) — avoid `git add -A` to prevent committing secrets or junk files.
2. Write a concise commit message (1-2 sentences) describing what changed and why.
3. Push to `main` (`git push origin main`).
4. Vercel will auto-deploy on push — no manual deploy needed.

## Do NOT batch

Don't accumulate many unrelated changes into one giant commit. Prefer small, focused commits so each deploy is easy to inspect and roll back if needed.
